elopment progresses.    A software application could use text analysis to show that all FIXITs are accounted for.------------------------------------------=====================------------------------------------------ [delete: after transition of template to repo instance]    In support of its educational goals, TSC LLC invents the word "FIXIT" as a placeholder for the    word chosen by the software development culture behind the ecosystem the developer works in.    The FSM of state about the FIXIT over Time are described by corporate project management.    The assignment of a FIXIT identifier instantiates a database entry that now will live forever.    The FIXIT database has a primary selection value for each individual and unique item.    References to values are made throughout repository metadata, without repeating the content.    Every software development organization makes up a set of conventions that must be followed.------------------------------------------ [delete: after transition of template to repo instance]    FIXIT keyword definition adopted for this project within this organization:        FppTnn   <format><project ID><M:missing | B:broken><integer 0-99>    The first letter defines the format of the rest of the keyword.  Every keyword in the database    that starts with 'F' will have exactly and completly the format described here.  This allows    corporate project management to separately share a single database across the organization.    Alternatively, experimental projects may still require oversight and documentation:        Xlllccssnn     <format><3-letter lab acronym><category><subcategory><integer 0-99>------------------------------------------ [edit:about this version]    This metadata file's content relates only to the version this metadata file describes.    Each FIXIT referenced is in a defined state, within the definition of the FIXIT-tracking FSM.    Any description of the FIXIT should be copie